APPLICATION FOR ATTACHMENT OF PROPERTY

IN THE COURT OF THE LEARNED SESSIONS JUDGE, JAIPUR

Sessions Case No. ______ of 2025

State of Rajasthan                                    … Applicant

Versus

Vijay Kumar Sharma                                       … Non-Applicant

APPLICATION FOR ATTACHMENT OF PROPERTY UNDER SECTION 452 OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023

MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:

1. That the applicant State has filed a chargesheet against the non-applicant for offences under Sections 420, 406, 409 and 120B BNS involving ₹5 crores.

2. That the non-applicant is likely to dispose of his properties to evade the consequences of the trial.

3. That the properties listed in Schedule-A belong to the non-applicant and were acquired using the proceeds of the alleged offence.

4. That attachment of these properties is necessary to ensure availability for restitution if the non-applicant is convicted.

PRAYER

It is therefore most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:

(a) Attach the properties described in Schedule-A;
(b) Prohibit the non-applicant from transferring, alienating or creating any third-party interest in these properties;
(c) Pass any other order as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper.

Place: Jaipur
Date: _______________

